# Normalise line endings in the repository, not just in the working tree.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true checks Lua,
# Markdown and JSON out with CRLF, and every tool that compares generated
# output against its committed file starts failing on a byte that git itself
# considers insignificant. That is not a cosmetic problem: it means the
# generated-file check reports "stale" on a tree where nothing is stale, so
# the check gets disabled or ignored, and then it stops catching the drift it
# exists to catch.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` makes LF the form in the repository AND in the working
# tree on every platform. Generated output is then byte-comparable everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary

# Source archives from a tag must not include the harness, tools, or 1.x docs.
# types/ is not listed: it ships.
test/ export-ignore
tools/ export-ignore
bench/ export-ignore
.github/ export-ignore
docs/archive/ export-ignore